@page "/docs/components"
@layout DocsLayout
@using MudBlazor

<PageTitle>Components — AgentBlazor Docs</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-article">
    <section class="docs-hero">
        <p class="docs-hero__eyebrow">Component Reference</p>
        <h1 class="docs-hero__title">Chat surfaces first, deterministic wrappers where they help.</h1>
        <p class="docs-hero__lede">
            AgentBlazor is not meant to turn an app into chat-driven clicking. The main UI surface is usually a route-scoped workflow plus
            either <code>AgentChatWidget</code> or <code>AgentChatSurface</code>. Deterministic wrappers are there when the host wants the agent
            to interact with specific MudBlazor-friendly controls safely.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Primary chat surfaces</h2>
                <p>These are the main host-facing components most apps start with.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-definition-grid">
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>AgentChatWidget</code></strong>
                <p>Floating assistant for ambient help, route-scoped prompts, and lightweight operator workflows.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>AgentChatSurface</code></strong>
                <p>Embedded chat panel for dashboards, workflow pages, and layouts where the assistant should stay visible.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>AgentChatPanel</code></strong>
                <p>Side-panel assistant for dense production screens such as queues, admin consoles, and operations dashboards.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-definition">
                <strong><code>AgentChatBar</code></strong>
                <p>Compact command entry for search, summaries, status updates, and quick workflow actions.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Production prompt examples</h2>
                <p>Use prompts that exercise real domain capability boundaries, approvals, and user context.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-card-grid">
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Executive summary</strong><p>Summarize this dashboard for an operations lead and call out the three riskiest items.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Operations queue</strong><p>Review this order queue, identify stuck orders, and recommend the safest next action.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Finance review</strong><p>Find invoices due this week, group them by risk, and draft a collector handoff note.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Approval gate</strong><p>Check whether order ABC123 can be submitted, explain missing approvals, and submit it only if policy allows.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Identity audit</strong><p>Summarize the current user-management page for an auditor and list accounts that need review.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Access remediation</strong><p>Find recently locked users, explain the likely causes, and draft a remediation checklist.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Release readiness</strong><p>Prepare a release-readiness checklist from deployment status, failed checks, and pending approvals.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Release handoff</strong><p>Compare staging and production status, list blockers, and draft the release manager handoff.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Incident support</strong><p>Draft a customer-support status update from the current incident screen and include open blockers.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Executive incident update</strong><p>Turn the current incident timeline into a short executive update with customer impact and next owner.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Inventory exception</strong><p>Review this inventory screen, identify low-stock exceptions, and create a purchasing follow-up note.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong>Claims workflow</strong><p>Inspect this claims workflow, identify missing evidence, and propose the next compliant action.</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Current deterministic UI wrappers</h2>
                <p>The demo component explorer focuses on the runtime wrappers that are already useful as host-owned control surfaces.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-card-grid">
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentDataGrid</code></strong><p>Sort, filter, page, and focus grid rows through deterministic actions.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentForm</code></strong><p>Validate, reset, and submit a host-owned form model.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentDialog</code></strong><p>Open, confirm, and close dialogs while the host still owns the content.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentNavMenu</code></strong><p>Expose safe route navigation actions from a host-defined menu.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentTabs</code></strong><p>Move between host-owned tabs without replacing the tab surface.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentSelect</code></strong><p>Set or clear values from a known option list.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentAutocomplete</code></strong><p>Drive query text and option selection in autocomplete surfaces.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentDatePicker</code></strong><p>Set one date from typed or natural-language input.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentDateRangePicker</code></strong><p>Apply a start and end date through one component contract.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentTreeView</code></strong><p>Expand, collapse, and select nodes inside a hierarchical host-owned tree.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentStepper</code></strong><p>Advance or jump through structured workflow steps.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentCommandBar</code></strong><p>Map natural-language requests onto a curated command surface.</p></div>
            <div class="docs-card"><strong><code>AgentFileUpload</code></strong><p>Attach, remove, and inspect files while preserving workflow policy.</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>When to use them</h2>
                <p>Keep the wrappers subordinate to the workflow model.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <ul class="docs-list">
            <li>Start with one workflow capability plus one chat surface.</li>
            <li>Add deterministic wrappers when the agent must safely manipulate a specific host-owned control.</li>
            <li>Prefer semantic workflow actions over exposing every possible control interaction directly.</li>
            <li>Use the component explorer as a reference surface after the workflow story is clear.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="docs-actions">
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/demo/components">Open Component Explorer</MudButton>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Selection rules</h2>
                <p>Choose the lightest surface that preserves host control.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-check-grid">
            <div class="docs-check">
                <strong>Use chat surfaces when</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>The workflow is primarily semantic.</li>
                    <li>The page already has its own host-owned UI.</li>
                    <li>You want route-scoped agent help without redesigning the screen.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-check">
                <strong>Use deterministic wrappers when</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>The agent must safely manipulate a specific control.</li>
                    <li>The host needs deterministic filtering, selection, or navigation actions.</li>
                    <li>You want proof of UI execution without handing over the full UI surface.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
        <div class="docs-section__header">
            <div>
                <h2>Read next</h2>
                <p>Go deeper into the live component reference or back up to workflow authoring.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-next-grid">
            <a href="/demo/components" class="docs-next-card">
                <strong>Component Explorer</strong>
                <p>Inspect each deterministic wrapper in a focused live example.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/docs/workflows" class="docs-next-card">
                <strong>Workflows</strong>
                <p>Return to the primary authoring model for route-scoped agent behavior.</p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
